        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Layout-design (topography) means the three-dimensional disposition, however expressed, of 
the elements of an integrated circuit (at least one of which is an active element) and of some or all of the interconnections of an integrated circuit, or such a three-dimensional disposition prepared for 
an integrated circuit intended for manufacture [Source: https://www.wipo.int/edocs/lexdocs/laws/en/hk/hk028en.pdf]</skos:definition>
