        <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://purl.org/coar/resource_type/542X-3S04"/>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Industrial designs are applied to a wide variety of industrial products and handicrafts. They refer to the ornamental or aesthetic aspects of a useful article,including compositions of lines or colors or any three-dimensional forms that give a special appearance to a product or handicraft. [Source: https://www.wipo.int/edocs/pubdocs/en/wipo_pub_943_2018.pdf]</skos:definition>
