        <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://schema.org/Map"/>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Any material representing the whole or part of the earth or any celestial body at any scale. Cartographic materials include two- and three-dimensional maps and plans (including maps of imaginary places); aeronautical, navigational, and celestial charts; atlases; globes; block diagrams; sections; aerial photographs with a cartographic purpose; bird&apos;s-eye views (map views), etc. [Source: http://www.loc.gov/marc/cfmap.html]</skos:definition>
